# Copyright (c) d-SEAMS developers
# Edits inside chemfiles' molfiles.tar.gz, applied by
# chemfiles-0.10.4-external-sources.sh before chemfiles unpacks the archive.
#
# molfile_plugin.h gains the three QM fields cpmdlogplugin and
# gaussianplugin write (have_esp, have_internals, shell_symmetry), and
# those two plugins are compiled instead of being wrapped in `#if false`.
#
# Hostile files. A truncated file, NUL bytes, an over-long line or a count
# the file cannot hold is an error, not a crash, a hang or an access
# outside a buffer:
#   ReadPARM7.h bounds every %s to its buffer, checks every fgets and
#   fscanf, reads an empty field of a short line as empty, and keeps the
#   POINTERS counts from overflowing. ReadPARM.h checks every read, the
#   header counts against the size of a regular file, and the residue,
#   molecule and bond indices. Both define S_ISREG where the C library
#   lacks it (MSVC). Their notice requires changes to the rest of the
#   file to be noted in comments; each file notes them.
#   parm7plugin and parmplugin stop at EOF while they look for a section.
#   gamessplugin, gaussianplugin, cpmdlogplugin and moldenplugin write
#   QM data only when the caller passes a QM timestep, keep frame indices
#   inside the frames they found, and bound their string scans and
#   copies; cpmdlogplugin's version check overflowed its word buffers.
#   cubeplugin stops at EOF while it skips the atom lines.
#   maeffplugin terminates the fields it prints and returns an empty bond
#   list without indexing it.
#   pqrplugin reads a line that starts with NUL; binposplugin and the
#   Gromacs.h TRJ and g96 readers check their atom counts and lengths.
#   dtrplugin checks each blob, label and CRC against its frame block,
#   frame and timekey sizes against the file, and the .ddparams path.
#   jsplugin checks its string tables and its block-I/O frame reads.
#   mdfplugin stops when the molecule section is truncated; dlpolyplugin
#   counts the atoms of a DL_POLY Classic CONFIG, whose header has none.
#   vtfplugin no longer walks off its line buffer, rejects a negative or
#   huge atom id, keeps its bond count when realloc fails, and refuses a
#   token that does not fit the molfile field. It reads a line char by
#   char: with fgets a NUL byte hid the line end, so a line depended on
#   how far the static buffer had grown on an earlier file and the second
#   open of a file could fail where the first had not. A continuation
#   line no longer keeps its backslash, comment and empty lines no longer
#   recurse, and the line numbers in errors restart with each file.
#   rst7plugin and tinkerplugin reject an atom count that does not fit
#   in the bytes left in the file and stop when a scan comes up short.
#   xsfplugin rejects an invalid PRIMCOORD count and stops at EOF in its
#   skip loops; xbgfplugin keeps CONECT rows inside bonds[16] and the
#   counts of its first pass.
#   abinitplugin and the VASP plugins bound their path copies and match
#   companion files only; hash.c hashes in unsigned arithmetic.
#   gamessplugin keeps gradient and coordinate rows inside the atoms it
#   counted and terminates the title, geometry and guess it copies.
#   bgfplugin and xbgfplugin parse each record from a NUL-padded copy, so
#   a short line is never read past its end, and count only atom records
#   as atoms; bgfplugin rejects more CONECT bonds than it counted.
#   The VASP POSCAR and XDATCAR readers reject atom counts that overflow
#   an int. endianswap.h and the Gromacs.h integer reads shift in
#   unsigned arithmetic.
#   gaussianplugin frees orb_indices and occupancies in close_gaussian_read
#   and on wavefunction failure, frees basis_set with num_basis_atoms, and
#   closes its handle on open failures. cpmdlogplugin and gamessplugin call
#   their close routines on open failures instead of leaking file handles,
#   file_name or qmdata_t. gromacsplugin calls mdio_close on gro and g96
#   open header failures.
#   Fuzz hardening (r4): abinitplugin bounds binary header counts against
#   file size, frees pawrhoij on error and validates typat[i] against
#   ntypat; ReadPARM frees prm and its arrays in ~ReadPARM() and frees
#   temporary buffers on error; moldenplugin, carplugin, cpmdplugin,
#   vaspposcarplugin, dmsplugin, Gromacs.h (mdio_timestep), vtfplugin,
#   mdfplugin and cpmdlogplugin (repeated ATOMS blocks) free allocations
#   and handles on error and close paths.
# VTF no longer refuses an atom id at a fixed 200000. The id has to
# fit in the signed index this plugin stores, and the allocation has
# to fit in size_t; a declared range of a million atoms is read.
# binpos rejects an atom count whose 12 bytes per atom are not left
# in the file, before it allocates the frame.
